Detective did it.

1183
00:52:45.900 --> 00:52:46.980
We mom detective it.

1184
00:52:47.040 --> 00:52:47.440
Detective did it.

1185
00:52:47.560 --> 00:52:47.900
Did it.

1186
00:52:48.240 --> 00:52:48.840
We did it.

1187
00:52:48.940 --> 00:52:49.940
We did it.

1188
00:52:52.480 --> 00:52:59.280
The location for this romantic reunion was the rooftop and stairwell of the Mayfair Hotel

1189
00:52:59.280 --> 00:53:00.720
in downtown Los Angeles.

1190
00:53:00.720 --> 00:53:03.280
If you're visiting, it's on 7th Street.

1191
00:53:03.940 --> 00:53:05.900
Brent shared with us about this scene.

1192
00:53:06.120 --> 00:53:08.800
I thought this was such a cool thing that he pointed out.

1193
00:53:08.980 --> 00:53:14.300
He talks about the tone of all the scenes and how this one is different from any other in

1194
00:53:14.300 --> 00:53:14.980
the whole episode.

1195
00:53:15.160 --> 00:53:15.720
Let's hear it.

1196
00:53:15.720 --> 00:53:21.720
I remember the energy of the actors in the A story was very fun.

1197
00:53:21.880 --> 00:53:28.820
It was Rainn Wilson, Ellie Kemper, Amy Ryan, and Steve Carell and were zipping around the

1198
00:53:28.820 --> 00:53:34.120
city and shooting these fun little set pieces, you know, in a parking lot, in a restaurant.

1199
00:53:34.120 --> 00:53:39.780
So the energy is very elevated until the scene on the rooftop.

1200
00:53:39.780 --> 00:53:46.420
And, you know, normally when you're shooting on location, there's a fair amount of shouting

1201
00:53:46.420 --> 00:53:47.560
among the crew.

1202
00:53:47.740 --> 00:53:49.700
They're trying to convey info, you know, outdoors.

1203
00:53:49.980 --> 00:53:55.020
But on this set, on that scene, the crew was whispering.

1204
00:53:55.480 --> 00:54:03.180
And I remember I walked onto set like a doofus yapping about something and I immediately went

1205
00:54:03.180 --> 00:54:03.720
silent.

1206
00:54:04.360 --> 00:54:07.940
Uh, and I looked around, why is everyone being so quiet?

1207
00:54:08.100 --> 00:54:15.040
And I saw Amy and Steve in the distance, you know, the crew had given them a lot of space

1208
00:54:15.040 --> 00:54:17.200
out of respect for what they were doing.

1209
00:54:17.420 --> 00:54:25.340
And they were great actors enacting real love between these two characters.

1210
00:54:25.340 --> 00:54:29.200
And the energy was sacred.

1211
00:54:30.260 --> 00:54:31.940
It's such a great scene.

1212
00:54:32.440 --> 00:54:34.880
They have this moment.

1213
00:54:35.360 --> 00:54:35.840
Yeah.

1214
00:54:36.060 --> 00:54:38.120
Where she just finally melts.

1215
00:54:38.360 --> 00:54:38.660
Mm-hmm.

1216
00:54:38.820 --> 00:54:39.800
And they kiss.

1217
00:54:40.220 --> 00:54:41.460
Erin sees it.

1218
00:54:41.600 --> 00:54:42.500
She's smiling.

1219
00:54:42.720 --> 00:54:47.260
And you just know, finally, finally, these two are back together.

1220
00:54:47.260 --> 00:54:53.760
And also, just as a fan of the show, I was a total audience member when I rewatched this.

1221
00:54:53.820 --> 00:54:59.800
And I was so emotional for Michael that he finally met his someone.

1222
00:55:00.060 --> 00:55:00.460
Mm-hmm.

1223
00:55:00.680 --> 00:55:02.240
Ah, so awesome.

1224
00:55:02.720 --> 00:55:05.360
We had a fan question, though.

1225
00:55:05.620 --> 00:55:07.540
Oh, well, this doesn't sound good.

1226
00:55:07.660 --> 00:55:07.880
What?

1227
00:55:08.180 --> 00:55:15.880
From Jade B in Nova Scotia, Canada, who said, how could Michael get lost in the small town

1228
00:55:15.880 --> 00:55:16.900
that he's from?

1229
00:55:17.260 --> 00:55:21.720
Why would he need to go to the top of a building to figure out where he is?

1230
00:55:21.940 --> 00:55:23.820
This never made sense to me.

1231
00:55:24.160 --> 00:55:25.620
And Mariah L.

1232
00:55:25.880 --> 00:55:27.580
from Colorado Springs agrees.

1233
00:55:28.740 --> 00:55:35.040
Mariah added, in The Client, Michael made fun of Jan for not knowing her way around Scranton

1234
00:55:35.040 --> 00:55:37.560
and said he spent his whole life here.

1235
00:55:37.740 --> 00:55:42.560
I realized that the writers wanted to find a way to get Holly to realize that Michael really

1236
00:55:42.560 --> 00:55:43.760
is her soup snake.

1237
00:55:43.760 --> 00:55:48.900
So maybe the story makes sense if you think that Michael is so depressed and out of sorts

1238
00:55:48.900 --> 00:55:51.900
that he really could get lost in his own hometown.

1239
00:55:53.020 --> 00:55:54.660
I have to say.

1240
00:55:55.300 --> 00:55:56.740
Why are you making that face?

1241
00:55:57.180 --> 00:56:01.840
She's making that face like, you know, like when your mom is maybe talking about someone,

1242
00:56:02.100 --> 00:56:05.500
but your mom doesn't normally gossip, but maybe she's saying something gossipy and she

1243
00:56:05.500 --> 00:56:07.940
makes a face like, bless his heart.

1244
00:56:07.940 --> 00:56:10.140
But I don't think they're wrong.

1245
00:56:10.440 --> 00:56:11.500
You don't think they're wrong.

1246
00:56:11.620 --> 00:56:14.100
I think it's a little bit of a stretch.

1247
00:56:14.580 --> 00:56:15.360
It is.

1248
00:56:15.740 --> 00:56:17.520
By the end, I don't care.

1249
00:56:17.740 --> 00:56:20.380
By the time they're kissing, I don't care.

1250
00:56:20.380 --> 00:56:24.160
But I will admit, I thought about it.

1251
00:56:24.300 --> 00:56:29.400
I thought, how is he so lost in his own city?

1252
00:56:29.820 --> 00:56:33.580
You know, what's interesting is when I watched it, I didn't think about that at all.

1253
00:56:33.800 --> 00:56:34.120
Really?

1254
00:56:34.460 --> 00:56:34.640
Yeah.

1255
00:56:34.640 --> 00:56:42.560
I watched it and I just thought, this is someone who is having a little bit of a life crisis,

1256
00:56:42.940 --> 00:56:43.200
right?

1257
